<title>GERMANY: MOTOR RACING-BERGER WINS GERMAN GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-BERGER WINS GERMAN GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>HOCKENHEIM, Germany 1997-07-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Gerhard Berger, driving a Benetton, won the German Grand Prix motor race on Sunday.  </p>
<p>Michael Schumacher of Germany finished second in a Ferrari,</p>
<p>with Finland's Mika Hakkinen third in a McLaren.</p>
<p>Jarno Trulli of Italy was fourth in a Prost, with Ralf</p>
<p>Schumacher of Germany fifth in a Jordan and Jean Alesi of France</p>
<p>sixth in a Benetton.</p>
<p>World drivers' championship standings (after 10 rounds):</p>
<p>  1. Michael Schumacher (Germany)	    53</p>
<p>  2. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada)	     43</p>
<p>  3. Jean Alesi (France)			 22</p>
<p>  4. Gerhard Berger  (Germany)		 20</p>
<p>  5. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany)	 19</p>
<p>  6. Eddie Irvine (Britain)		    18</p>
<p>  7. Olivier Panis (France)		    15</p>
<p>  8 equal. David Coulthard (Britain)	 14</p>
<p>  8 equal. Mika Hakkinen (Finland)	   14</p>
<p>  9. Ralf Schumacher (Germany)		  9</p>
<p> 10. Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy)	     8</p>
<p> 11. Johnny Herbert (Britain)		   7</p>
<p> 12. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil)		6</p>
<p> 13. Alexander Wurz (Austria		    4</p>
<p> 14. Jarno Trulli (Italy			  3</p>
<p> 15. Mika Salo (Finland)			  2</p>
<p> 16 equal. Nicola Larini (Italy)		1</p>
<p> 16 equal. Shinji Nakano (Japan)		1</p>
<p> 16 equal. Damon Hill (Britain)		 1</p>
